        for over 15 years in clinical settings in Hong Kong and the UK.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Accreditation grid — 4 columns -->
    <div class="accred-grid">

      <!-- 15+ Years -->
      <div class="accred-card">
        <div class="accred-stat">15+</div>
        <p class="accred-name">Years' Clinical<br>Experience</p>
        <p class="accred-role">Hong Kong &amp; UK practice</p>
      </div>

      <!-- BAcC -->
      <div class="accred-card">
        <img class="accred-logo" src="/images/bacc-member-logo.png" alt="British Acupuncture Council Member" loading="lazy" style="max-width:180px" />
        <p class="accred-name">British Acupuncture<br>Council</p>
        <p class="accred-role">Registered Member<br>Nos. 963087 &amp; 963093</p>
      </div>

      <!-- ATCM -->
      <div class="accred-card">
        <img class="accred-logo" src="/images/atcm-logo.png" alt="Association of Traditional Chinese Medicine &amp; Acupuncture" loading="lazy" />
        <p class="accred-name">Association of TCM<br>&amp; Acupuncture</p>
        <p class="accred-role">Professional Member<br>FM0250004 &amp; FM0250005</p>
      </div>

      <!-- PSA -->
      <div class="accred-card">
        <img
          class="accred-logo"
          src="/images/psa-logo.png"
          alt="Professional Standards Authority"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <p class="accred-name">Professional Standards<br>Authority</p>
        <p class="accred-role">Accredited Register<br>relationship via BAcC</p>
      </div>

    </div>

    <!-- Insurance logos -->
    <div class="accred-divider">
      <p class="accred-divider-label">Also recognised by UK health insurers</p>
      <div class="insurer-strip">
        <img src="/images/axa-health-logo.png" alt="AXA Health" style="height:36px" loading="lazy" />
        <img src="/images/vitality-health-logo.webp" alt="Vitality Health" style="height:36px" loading="lazy" />
        <img src="/images/aviva-health-logo.png" alt="Aviva Health" style="height:36px" loading="lazy" />
        <img src="/images/wpa-logo.png" alt="WPA" style="height:36px" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>


<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════
     §6 CLINICAL APPROACH
═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="section-soft">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="grid-2-lg" style="gap:5rem">

      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Our Approach</p>
        <h2>How We Work</h2>

        <div class="pull-quote">
          <p>"Clear clinical communication, structured assessment, and evidence-conscious
          treatment — delivered at our Reading and Wimbledon clinics."</p>
        </div>

        <p>
          Every patient interaction begins with a structured assessment combining
          traditional pulse and tongue diagnosis with a thorough review of your medical
          history, lifestyle, and presenting symptoms.
        </p>

        <!-- Frequency reference — always visible, scannable -->
        <div style="margin-top:1.5rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--r-md);overflow:hidden">
          <div style="padding:0.7rem 1.2rem;background:var(--cream);border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)">
            <p style="font-size:0.76rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted);margin:0">Typical Treatment Frequency</p>
          </div>
          {[
            ["Acute pain or injury",     "2–3× per week for 2 weeks, then reassess"],
            ["Chronic musculoskeletal",  "Weekly for 4–6 weeks, then bi-weekly"],
            ["Women's health",           "Weekly, timed to menstrual cycle phase"],
            ["Skin conditions",          "Weekly 6–8 weeks; herbal review every 2 weeks"],
          ].map(([cond, freq], i) => (
            <div style={`display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:1rem;padding:0.7rem 1.2rem;font-size:0.87rem;${i < 3 ? "border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)" : ""}`}>
              <span style="font-weight:600;color:var(--navy)">{cond}</span>
              <span style="color:var(--muted);text-align:right">{freq}</span>
            </div>
          ))}
          <div style="padding:0.5rem 1.2rem;font-size:0.76rem;color:var(--muted);background:var(--cream)">
            Indicative benchmarks. Your practitioner adjusts based on your clinical response.
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Progressive disclosure for detailed clinical approach -->
        <details class="expand-detail">
          <summary class="expand-summary">
            Read about our full clinical approach
            <span class="expand-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </summary>
          <div class="expand-body">
            <h3>Diagnosis before treatment</h3>
            <p>
              We do not prescribe a treatment plan before completing a structured clinical
              assessment. Combining traditional pulse and tongue diagnosis with a thorough
              review of your Western medical history, lifestyle factors, and presenting
              symptoms, we identify the root systemic pattern — not just the presenting symptom.
            </p>
            <h3>Session-by-session adaptation</h3>
            <p>
              Your acupuncture point selection, manual therapy techniques, and herbal
              prescription are reassessed at every appointment and adjusted to match your
              current clinical picture. This session-by-session responsiveness is how we keep
              treatment matched to your presentation, rather than repeating a fixed protocol.
            </p>
            <h3>Integrated protocols where appropriate</h3>
            <p>
              When clinically indicated, we combine modalities within a single session — for
              example, acupuncture for neurological pain regulation combined with Tui Na for
              soft tissue and joint work. Every combination is determined by your practitioner's
              assessment, not by a fixed package offering.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>

      <!-- Right: stats + image -->
      <div style="display:grid;gap:1.5rem;align-content:start">

        <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1px;background:var(--border);border-radius:var(--r-lg);overflow:hidden">
          {[
            { val: "4.9★",  label: "Google Reviews" },
            { val: "2",     label: "UK clinic locations" },
            { val: "EN/粵", label: "Bilingual care" },
            { val: "No GP", label: "referral needed" },
          ].map(({ val, label }) => (
            <div style="background:var(--white);padding:1.5rem;text-align:center">
              <span style="display:block;font-family:var(--serif);font-size:2rem;color:var(--navy);line-height:1;margin-bottom:0.35rem">{val}</span>
              <span style="font-size:0.76rem;color:var(--muted);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.08em">{label}</span>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>

        <img
          src="/images/acupuncture-abdomen-treatment.webp"
          alt="Acupuncture needles being inserted into a patient's abdomen"
          style="width:100%;height:260px;object-fit:cover;border-radius:var(--r-lg)"
          loading="lazy"
        />

        <div style="background:var(--navy);border-radius:var(--r-md);padding:1.3rem">
          <p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.02rem;font-style:italic;color:#f0ece2;line-height:1.6;margin:0">
            "Same-week appointments available. New patients welcome — no referral needed."
          </p>
          <a class="btn btn-gold btn-sm" href="https://wa.me/447301949686" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" style="margin-top:0.9rem">WhatsApp Us Now</a>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════
     §7 CONDITIONS WE TREAT
═══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Conditions We Treat</p>
      <h2>Where Our Expertise Makes the Most Difference</h2>
      <p>
        Our clinical focus is deliberately narrow — areas where acupuncture, manual
        therapy, and herbal medicine are most commonly used together as part of patient care.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid-3" style="margin-bottom:2.5rem">
      <div style="padding:1.6rem;background:var(--cream);border-radius:var(--r-lg);border:1px solid rgba(192,152,90,0.2)">
        <p style="font-size:1.4rem;margin-bottom:0.5rem">🦴</p>
        <h3 style="font-size:1.05rem">Chronic Pain &amp; Spinal Problems</h3>
        <p style="font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--muted)">
          Lumbar disc herniation, sciatica, cervical spondylosis, and sacroiliac dysfunction.
          Acupuncture and bone-setting are often used together as part of care for these conditions.
        </p>
        <a class="more-link" href="/herniated-disc">Herniated disc &amp; sciatica</a>
      </div>
      <div style="padding:1.6rem;background:var(--cream);border-radius:var(--r-lg);border:1px solid rgba(192,152,90,0.2)">
        <p style="font-size:1.4rem;margin-bottom:0.5rem">🌸</p>
        <h3 style="font-size:1.05rem">Women's Health &amp; Hormonal Balance</h3>
        <p style="font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--muted)">
          Postnatal recovery, menstrual irregularity, PCOS, perimenopause, and fertility support.
          Your practitioner will assess whether acupuncture or herbal medicine may be appropriate
          for your individual circumstances.
        </p>
        <a class="more-link" href="/contact">Enquire about Women's Health</a>
      </div>
      <div style="padding:1.6rem;background:var(--cream);border-radius:var(--r-lg);border:1px solid rgba(192,152,90,0.2)">
        <p style="font-size:1.4rem;margin-bottom:0.5rem">🏃</p>
        <h3 style="font-size:1.05rem">Sports Injuries &amp; Recovery</h3>
        <p style="font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--muted)">
          Ligament sprains, tendinopathy, muscle tears, and repetitive strain. Tui Na and
          acupuncture are commonly used as part of rehabilitation programmes for recreational
          and competitive athletes.
        </p>
        <a class="more-link" href="/sports-injuries">Sports Injuries</a>
